1
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:48,339
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:58,975
2017
PRAGUE

3
00:00:59,059 --> 00:01:01,770
<i>We are at the Prague Harmonie</i>
<i>International Competition finals venue.</i>

4
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:05,482
<i>Today is the final round,</i>
<i>featuring the two finalists.</i>

5
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:09,402
<i>Following their exceptional</i>
<i>semifinal performances,</i>

6
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:12,322
<i>all attention is focused</i>
<i>on today's event.</i>

7
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:39,974
Let go of me!

8
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,267
I said let go!

9
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,561
Where are we going now?

10
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:09,189
Excuse me.

11
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:10,523
Stop, stop!

12
00:03:10,607 --> 00:03:12,275
I want to go to the toilet!

13
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,944
Are you listening to me?

14
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:17,071
I said I need to go to the restroom!

15
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,240
Cut the crap!

16
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:21,993
Or else I'll put a bullet
through your head.

17
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,318
Watch it!

18
00:03:55,401 --> 00:03:56,486
No, you watch it.

19
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:57,987
Don't get blood splatter in the car.

20
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:02,825
Who do you think you are?
Don't tell me what to do.

21
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:07,658
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

22
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:09,327
<i>We will now present</i>

23
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,829
an award to Kang Pi-o…

24
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,081
6 MONTHS AGO

25
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:15,249
…for bringing honor
to Korea Arts High School.

26
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:19,712
Kang Pi-o, please come to the podium.

27
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:21,672
{\an8}EPISODE 1

28
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:26,135
{\an8}Is all this necessary?

29
00:06:26,219 --> 00:06:27,470
{\an8}You performed so much better.

30
00:06:40,316 --> 00:06:41,275
{\an8}"The above student

31
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:45,321
{\an8}is hereby commended
for elevating our school's reputation

32
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:46,906
{\an8}by winning the grand prize

33
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:50,326
{\an8}at the 27th Lake Erie
International Junior Competition."

34
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:59,168
{\an8}CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION
NAME: KANG PI-O

35
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:06,884
DROP OUT, BASTARD
LEAVE, ILLEGITIMATE CHILD

36
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,261
Han-rim, he's over here.

37
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:15,226
Hey, did you throw this in the trash?

38
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:18,729
You're so damn full of yourself.

39
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,942
The whole school gathered
for the stupid ceremony

40
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:24,944
because you won some competition.

41
00:07:25,027 --> 00:07:26,946
You crossed the line, don't you think?

42
00:07:30,700 --> 00:07:31,534
Hey.

43
00:07:31,617 --> 00:07:33,536
Are we just here to make you look good?

44
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:37,081
Well, I suppose winning a competition

45
00:07:37,915 --> 00:07:41,252
is nothing to Kang Seung-woon's grandson.

46
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:44,046
You think that's funny?

47
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,339
Let us in on the joke.

48
00:07:48,926 --> 00:07:52,096
Do you think it's my fault
you guys didn't place?

49
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:54,557
If you're so bitter about not placing,

50
00:07:55,349 --> 00:07:59,562
try to spend less time picking fights
and more time practicing.

51
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:02,648
Seriously?

52
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:05,902
What about you?

53
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:08,321
Aren't you trying to prove yourself

54
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:11,157
because you're bitter
about your family background?

55
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:14,869
-Hey!
-What the hell?

56
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:17,538
What are you guys doing?

57
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,540
-Jeez, it's her again.
-That scared me.

58
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:24,504
Why are you guys messing with Pi-o again?

59
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,381
Snap out of it, Hong Jae-in.

60
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,301
Stop letting this jerk use you.

61
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:34,180
Let's go.

62
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:35,389
Hey, wait up.

63
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:43,856
Wait, Pi-o!

64
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,859
How many times do I have to tell you?

65
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:49,946
Try to be just a little more humble.

66
00:08:50,613 --> 00:08:53,199
Those guys are jealous of you as it is.

67
00:08:53,282 --> 00:08:55,409
You didn't have to
throw away that certificate.

68
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:57,745
Or you could've thrown it away at home.

69
00:08:59,872 --> 00:09:02,625
Why should I have to
cater to everyone else's feelings?

70
00:09:05,878 --> 00:09:07,004
Are you…

71
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:09,674
a sociopath?

72
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,178
Why don't you tell me what you want?

73
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:15,680
Me?

74
00:09:16,514 --> 00:09:17,890
I don't want anything.

75
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:19,767
Oh, yeah? Never mind then.

76
00:09:20,935 --> 00:09:23,521
-Actually, I--
-Sorry.

77
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:24,730
Find someone else.

78
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:26,774
You didn't even hear me out.

79
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:28,818
Weren't you going to ask me
to be your accompanist?

80
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:30,611
How did you know?

81
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,407
Hey, Pi-o!

82
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:36,742
Just hear me out.

83
00:09:39,662 --> 00:09:41,080
Pi-o.

84
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:45,126
I wouldn't ask you if I didn't have to.

85
00:09:45,209 --> 00:09:47,128
But none of the others are any good.

86
00:09:47,753 --> 00:09:49,964
There's no way I can play with them.

87
00:09:50,798 --> 00:09:51,799
I'm busy.

88
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,510
It's not a lot. Just three…

89
00:09:55,303 --> 00:09:56,596
No, wait.

90
00:09:57,471 --> 00:09:58,389
Just twice.

91
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:03,269
Come on, it won't take up
much of your time.

92
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:05,021
Hey!

93
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:07,982
I'm practically begging you here!

94
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:15,364
I didn't want to say this,

95
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:17,158
but we're not on the same level.

96
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:18,993
Playing together
would only expose you.

97
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:20,911
Why play a concerto like that?

98
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:25,291
That's a pretty harsh thing to say.

99
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,460
But that's my point.

100
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:31,255
I'm asking you
to help me out with your skills.

101
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,051
No. I don't want to.

102
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:37,094
Hey, Kang Pi-o!

103
00:10:41,849 --> 00:10:43,851
Hey, I'm talking to you!

104
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:16,801
Right.

105
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,179
This is exactly why

106
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:22,014
I can't lose you.

107
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:26,394
How do you capture Schumann so perfectly?

108
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:48,541
Pi-o.

109
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,797
Forget the accompaniment.

110
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:57,633
Let's just get married.

111
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:00,720
I seriously need to

112
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,597
listen to you play forever.

113
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:11,814
Will you just leave already?

114
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:14,066
Hey, I'm totally serious!

115
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,111
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

116
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:41,469
Where are you going?

117
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:05,576
Get up, Choi Jeong-yo!

118
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:08,162
Everyone, gather around.

119
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:13,501
I want an answer now.

120
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:15,753
What will you do
about the music practical?

121
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:18,839
You really can't play a single instrument?

122
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:21,091
-Come on, a practical?
-We can't.

123
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,676
I told you a million times.

124
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:26,055
Bring a triangle or something
and take the practical.

125
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:31,393
Here's the alternative.

126
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:35,189
My friend called and said
they need to fill the seats.

127
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:38,692
If you attend,
I'll give you credit for the practical.

128
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:39,819
Is that better?

129
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,362
What a shame. I'll pass.

130
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,030
What do you mean?

131
00:13:43,113 --> 00:13:45,449
I'm going out of my way
to cut you some slack.

132
00:13:45,533 --> 00:13:47,117
No one goes to those things anymore.

133
00:13:48,035 --> 00:13:49,912
This is way too much pressure.

134
00:13:49,995 --> 00:13:51,956
Why don't you just give up on us?

135
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,958
-Choi Jeong-yo!
-Here!

136
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,547
I don't want to go.

137
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:08,138
Hello, Rider Jo!

138
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,473
That idiot.

139
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:14,395
Man, look at you being responsible
and coming to school every day.

140
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,772
Get into any trouble today?

141
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:20,025
Want me to get into serious trouble
and get expelled?

142
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,111
You're too chicken to do that.

143
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,865
-Hop on.
-All right, let's go.

144
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:34,915
Get your fast cash!

145
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,792
NEED CASH FAST?

146
00:14:41,213 --> 00:14:42,381
A real man

147
00:14:43,591 --> 00:14:46,927
never forgets the hard times
he went through.

148
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:48,679
You boys.

149
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:52,391
When you make it big someday,

150
00:14:52,975 --> 00:14:54,268
remember me, okay?

151
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:55,185
Thank you, sir.

152
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:58,522
-Here.
-Thank you!

153
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,065
You punk.

154
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:01,901
I gave you a bit extra.

155
00:15:01,984 --> 00:15:03,485
-Here. Work hard.
-Thank you.

156
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,571
-You can all be successful.
-Thank you, sir.

157
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:09,033
Hey, Jeong-yo.

158
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,620
Eat up, okay?

159
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,747
You've lost weight.

160
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:16,624
By the way, Jeong-yo,

161
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:19,835
tell your father to pay up what he owes.

162
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,587
I'm broke as hell right now.

163
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:24,298
Look at us,
just eating <i>jjajangmyeon </i>every day.

164
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:28,385
Hello, this is Happy Loan.

165
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:30,262
-How are you, ma'am?
-Forget it.

166
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,056
-I mean, miss.
-Take it, you punk.

167
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:34,266
Don't be so stubborn.

168
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:35,559
Hurry up and eat.

169
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:47,655
{\an8}MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
TRADITIONAL MARKET

170
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:56,956
{\an8}MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

171
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:29,113
I told you to stop bringing me money,
damn it!

172
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,490
It makes it impossible

173
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,411
for me to hate you in peace.

174
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:41,709
Hey.

175
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:44,878
Do you feel sorry for me?

176
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:48,674
Is that why you keep bringing me money?

177
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:52,094
You're pitiful too.

178
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:55,597
And so am I.

179
00:16:56,682 --> 00:17:00,185
You're pitiful…

180
00:17:02,646 --> 00:17:04,815
and I'm pitiful too.

181
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:22,207
{\an8}GRAND PRIZE
PIANO, CHOI JEONG-YO

182
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,359
NOTICE OF OVERDUE HEALTH INSURANCE PREMIUM

183
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:52,112
NOTICE OF OVERDUE INTEREST

184
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,087
-Hello.
-Hey.

185
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:11,423
-Taking good care of yourself?
-Yes, ma'am.

186
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:19,700
It feels amazing
to finally watch a proper performance.

187
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:23,829
How is Hyun-soo still so good
after all this time?

188
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:25,330
Most people lose their touch

189
00:19:25,414 --> 00:19:28,375
and just go through the motions
when they hit middle age.

190
00:19:29,751 --> 00:19:33,172
Maestro Kang made it so obvious
he was fond of Hyun-soo.

191
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:37,134
He won't even shake hands
if he doesn't like a performance.

192
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:41,889
A conductor shouldn't be
so transparent with his emotions.

193
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:43,640
It intimidates the people he works with.

194
00:19:45,976 --> 00:19:48,478
Yes, I suppose you're right.

195
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,482
Did you find an orchestra
for the concerto?

196
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:54,276
Oh, I have meetings next week

197
00:19:54,359 --> 00:19:57,571
with the Gyeongseong Philharmonic
and the Seonghan Philharmonic.

198
00:19:58,697 --> 00:20:00,407
Don't worry about a thing.

199
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:03,327
It's Pi-o. Who would turn him down?

200
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:06,413
I know you're busy
trying to win Hyun-soo over,

201
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:10,584
but if you neglect my son because of it,
I'll terminate our contract.

202
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:15,339
Come on. I wouldn't do that.

203
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:19,051
The entire company is focused on him.

204
00:20:21,595 --> 00:20:25,224
By the way, Jae-in said
you refused to be her accompanist.

205
00:20:26,850 --> 00:20:27,893
I'm sorry.

206
00:20:29,102 --> 00:20:31,021
Don't worry about it.
You made the right call.

207
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:35,317
Honestly, it'd benefit me more
if you spent that time practicing

208
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,902
than helping that brat out.

209
00:20:38,487 --> 00:20:40,989
And I don't want your mom
to come after me.

210
00:20:44,534 --> 00:20:46,161
I'd love to stay here.

211
00:20:46,828 --> 00:20:49,248
Performing with you today made me realize

212
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:52,668
what a privilege it is to play with you.

213
00:20:52,751 --> 00:20:54,836
Not at all, sir. You're too kind.

214
00:20:58,799 --> 00:20:59,800
You're home.

215
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:06,473
Hey, you're here.

216
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:12,479
Mr. Kang felt it was too early
to call it a night, so…

217
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:16,024
I enjoyed your performance today.

218
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,026
Thanks.

219
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,112
I heard Hyun-jeong's company
made you an offer.

220
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:22,572
Yes, I've decided to stay
in Korea for a while.

221
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:26,451
You've probably had dinner already,
so join us for a drink.

222
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,536
No, thank you.

223
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:33,208
You must be Pi-o.

224
00:21:37,129 --> 00:21:38,630
I've heard a lot about you.

225
00:21:38,714 --> 00:21:40,132
You took first place at Lake Erie?

226
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:44,720
As expected of your grandson, sir.

227
00:21:44,803 --> 00:21:47,389
He must've inherited your musical talent.

228
00:21:47,472 --> 00:21:48,890
Stop talking nonsense.

229
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:54,062
Don't give a talentless kid false hope,
and be careful with your praise.

230
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:58,108
Empty praise does more harm than good.

231
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,277
-Father.
-Go upstairs.

232
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:03,864
I don't want to ruin my night.

233
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:21,214
How could you say that
in front of Hyun-soo?

234
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,175
You can hate me all you want!

235
00:22:23,258 --> 00:22:25,510
But why say things like that
with Pi-o right there?

236
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:29,598
Don't expect me to live through your child
the way you do.

237
00:22:29,681 --> 00:22:33,143
But he's still your grandson,
and he's my son!

238
00:22:33,226 --> 00:22:34,353
Don't fool yourself.

239
00:22:35,228 --> 00:22:38,023
The only reason I let you two live here

240
00:22:38,106 --> 00:22:41,068
is out of pity for you
trying to play mother,

241
00:22:41,151 --> 00:22:42,944
not because I accept him as my grandson.

242
00:22:43,028 --> 00:22:45,364
Why can't you accept him? Why?

243
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:48,700
You expect me to accept a kid
with no known father as my grandson?

244
00:22:49,951 --> 00:22:53,163
But more than that,
he doesn't have what it takes.

245
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,665
Stop wasting your time
on that hopeless fool

246
00:22:55,749 --> 00:22:57,584
and focus on your own life!

247
00:22:58,710 --> 00:22:59,711
Father!

248
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:08,220
Start playing.

249
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,753
Hail, Mary, full of grace,
the Lord is with thee.

250
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:46,341
Blessed art thou amongst women,

251
00:23:46,425 --> 00:23:48,760
and blessed is
the fruit of thy womb, Jesus.

252
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:52,139
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

253
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:54,516
pray for us sinners,

254
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,269
now and at the hour of our death.

255
00:23:58,186 --> 00:23:59,104
Amen.

256
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:03,900
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

257
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:06,736
pray for us sinners,

258
00:24:08,363 --> 00:24:10,282
now and at the hour of our death.

259
00:24:11,116 --> 00:24:12,284
Amen.

260
00:24:12,367 --> 00:24:14,327
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

261
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,414
pray for us sinners,

262
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:21,126
now and at the hour of our death.

263
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,086
Amen.

264
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:26,673
Come in.

265
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:42,230
I have something to tell you.

266
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:46,610
Do you really think
I don't have what it takes?

267
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:50,363
Or do you just want to think that
because you hate me?

268
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:54,951
I've looked up to you since I was little.

269
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:59,414
I gave it everything I had
just to earn one compliment from you.

270
00:25:00,290 --> 00:25:02,959
But even after I took first place
in so many competitions,

271
00:25:03,043 --> 00:25:05,378
you never once glanced at me.

272
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:07,839
If it's because you hate me--

273
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:09,341
So you're asking…

274
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:18,725
why I'd put down a talented kid like you
just because of my personal feelings.

275
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:21,978
Is that it?

276
00:25:56,555 --> 00:25:57,889
What do you think you're doing?

277
00:26:02,602 --> 00:26:04,896
You think I care to see you
show off your technique?

278
00:26:56,573 --> 00:26:59,743
You have the nerve to complain
about fairness with skills like this?

279
00:27:01,244 --> 00:27:05,040
With a performance
full of nothing but hollow desire?

280
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:10,962
The people I despise the most in the world

281
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:13,173
are those who mistake
the greatness of their music

282
00:27:13,715 --> 00:27:16,551
for proof that they themselves are great.

283
00:27:17,302 --> 00:27:18,345
Unfortunately,

284
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:21,389
you're one of them.

285
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:26,728
I've never thought of myself that way!

286
00:27:27,312 --> 00:27:29,397
All I wanted was your approval.

287
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:31,149
Is that so wrong?

288
00:27:35,779 --> 00:27:36,696
Just once.

289
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:39,324
Give me one more chance.

290
00:27:40,116 --> 00:27:42,619
If you still say no
after I play for you again,

291
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:45,789
I'll quit playing the piano.

292
00:27:45,872 --> 00:27:47,666
I don't have time to spare for you.

293
00:27:48,166 --> 00:27:49,751
Even for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

294
00:27:51,961 --> 00:27:53,421
You arrogant fool.

295
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:58,009
Winning a few competitions
has made you laughably arrogant.

296
00:28:01,888 --> 00:28:03,014
What if I do get to play there?

297
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:05,934
Will you come watch me perform?

298
00:28:06,810 --> 00:28:07,852
Fine.

299
00:28:08,436 --> 00:28:10,397
Let's see you try.

300
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:13,441
But if I still feel the same way then…

301
00:28:15,443 --> 00:28:17,946
you'll need to take responsibility
for what you said.

302
00:28:25,995 --> 00:28:27,247
<i>That's absurd.</i>

303
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:31,501
You can't change teachers
right before the competition.

304
00:28:32,419 --> 00:28:35,004
You know how important it is
to get into Professor Seo's inner circle.

305
00:28:35,088 --> 00:28:37,424
That's not important to me.

306
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:39,551
I need a real teacher

307
00:28:40,635 --> 00:28:41,970
who can teach me properly.

308
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:43,054
How could that…

309
00:28:45,473 --> 00:28:47,100
How could that not be important?

310
00:28:47,183 --> 00:28:49,102
It all comes down to business in the end.

311
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:54,023
And of all people,
why does it have to be Hyun-soo?

312
00:28:55,275 --> 00:28:58,778
He has exceptional talent,
but he's still only a performer.

313
00:28:59,696 --> 00:29:01,322
I told Grandfather

314
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:04,033
that he'd see me perform
at the Noblesse Classical Concert.

315
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:08,329
And I told him I'd quit the piano
if he still didn't approve.

316
00:29:08,413 --> 00:29:09,789
Do you really think Professor Seo

317
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:12,000
could pull that off?

318
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:14,169
Why did you say that
without talking to me…

319
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:15,795
Pi-o!

320
00:29:18,631 --> 00:29:19,549
Are you off to school?

321
00:29:27,098 --> 00:29:27,974
Have a good day.

322
00:29:36,649 --> 00:29:38,276
I have to say, Pi-o is smart.

323
00:29:39,068 --> 00:29:41,946
He knows exactly what he needs.

324
00:29:44,532 --> 00:29:47,160
You talk like
it doesn't concern you at all.

325
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:51,831
Why are you being so hostile?

326
00:29:52,999 --> 00:29:54,042
Let's be honest.

327
00:29:54,834 --> 00:29:58,338
Everyone in the music industry knows
Professor Seo is overrated.

328
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:03,009
I think Pi-o made the right call.

329
00:30:03,885 --> 00:30:05,595
If only Father had supported him,

330
00:30:05,678 --> 00:30:08,181
he wouldn't have had to
turn to Professor Seo.

331
00:30:09,849 --> 00:30:12,936
How could you possibly know what it's like
to be completely powerless, Mother?

332
00:30:56,563 --> 00:30:58,064
You're really good.

333
00:30:58,815 --> 00:31:00,817
I can't find a single flaw.

334
00:31:01,568 --> 00:31:03,194
Why did you come to me?

335
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:04,612
You don't need my help.

336
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:06,698
That's not true.

337
00:31:08,783 --> 00:31:11,035
You didn't like how I played.

338
00:31:12,912 --> 00:31:14,330
That isn't true.

339
00:31:16,916 --> 00:31:20,587
You should just learn from Professor Seo.

340
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:31,222
What did he say?

341
00:31:54,329 --> 00:31:56,956
<i>You should just learn from Professor Seo.</i>

342
00:31:59,250 --> 00:32:02,629
<i>You have the nerve to complain</i>
<i>about fairness with skills like this?</i>

343
00:32:03,671 --> 00:32:07,342
<i>With a performance</i>
<i>full of nothing but hollow desire?</i>

344
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:15,642
{\an8}ARTS & MUSIC HALL

345
00:32:41,042 --> 00:32:42,210
Man, I'm dying here.

346
00:32:44,837 --> 00:32:46,422
I can't listen to this anymore.

347
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:49,425
-Let's go.
-All right.

348
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:52,637
-Hurry up before the teacher sees us.
-Okay.

349
00:32:54,180 --> 00:32:55,431
Let's go.

350
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,199
Come on, Jeong-yo. Let's go.

351
00:33:14,575 --> 00:33:15,785
You guys go ahead.

352
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:49,777
KANG PI-O (17 YEARS OLD)
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

353
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:51,821
Kang Pi-o?

354
00:33:55,491 --> 00:33:58,536
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

355
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:02,915
What's your name?

356
00:34:02,999 --> 00:34:04,333
Kang Pi-o.

357
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:34,113
{\an8}KANG PI-O
1ST PRIZE

358
00:34:34,197 --> 00:34:35,698
Look over here, please!

359
00:34:35,782 --> 00:34:38,034
-Pi-o!
-Over here!

360
00:34:38,117 --> 00:34:39,368
Can we get a photo?

361
00:34:39,452 --> 00:34:41,329
They know how amazing you are, don't they?

362
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,122
-Look over here!
-Please, Pi-o!

363
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,792
Why are you so upset?

364
00:34:46,542 --> 00:34:49,337
Kang Pi-o, the perfectionist.

365
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,048
What didn't you like?

366
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:54,175
{\an8}My cadenza was a disaster.

367
00:34:54,258 --> 00:34:56,719
{\an8}CADENZA: A VIRTUOSIC, IMPROVISED SOLO
NEAR THE END OF A CONCERTO MOVEMENT

368
00:34:56,803 --> 00:34:58,346
{\an8}It wasn't like that during practice.

369
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:03,518
You know, I've been thinking.

370
00:35:04,477 --> 00:35:06,938
Overdoing it in the cadenza

371
00:35:07,647 --> 00:35:09,148
is a bit tacky.

372
00:35:09,232 --> 00:35:10,691
Playing it with a lighter touch

373
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,528
actually blended better
with the orchestra today.

374
00:35:14,529 --> 00:35:17,115
A pianist shouldn't
race ahead of the music, right?

375
00:35:24,038 --> 00:35:25,456
-Hey, Pi-o!
-Pi-o!

376
00:35:25,540 --> 00:35:27,458
-Hello, ma'am.
-Get in, kids.

377
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:30,002
I left my sheet music in the waiting room.

378
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:31,462
Go get it.

379
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:35,800
Wait for me.

380
00:35:37,009 --> 00:35:39,178
5TH CHEONGUN
INTERNATIONAL MUSIC COMPETITION

381
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,141
Are you sure you can cut class like this?

382
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:44,976
Your teacher won't say anything?

383
00:35:46,060 --> 00:35:50,398
My future husband's
military exemption is on the line.

384
00:35:51,107 --> 00:35:52,108
You think class matters?

385
00:35:53,025 --> 00:35:53,860
Cut it out.

386
00:35:59,949 --> 00:36:00,783
Who's that?

387
00:36:02,076 --> 00:36:03,411
Who's playing so well?

388
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:10,751
Damn it.

389
00:36:10,835 --> 00:36:12,587
Hey, Pi-o.

390
00:36:13,838 --> 00:36:15,798
Find out who that is.

391
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:17,842
Hello, teacher.

392
00:36:18,551 --> 00:36:19,927
I caught a cold.

393
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:27,602
KANG PI-O

394
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:47,788
Who are you?

395
00:36:47,872 --> 00:36:50,249
Who the hell are you,
looking at my sheet music like that?

396
00:36:51,876 --> 00:36:52,752
I'm sorry.

397
00:36:54,003 --> 00:36:55,463
I didn't mean to.

398
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:58,424
Hey.

399
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:02,929
Don't you remember me?

400
00:37:03,638 --> 00:37:05,056
Who are you?

401
00:37:07,308 --> 00:37:09,268
Never mind. I'm sorry.

402
00:37:10,102 --> 00:37:12,271
By the way,
your cadenza sounded a bit dry.

403
00:37:12,355 --> 00:37:13,606
Was that intentional?

404
00:37:20,196 --> 00:37:21,364
I just…

405
00:37:22,865 --> 00:37:25,660
That's just what I thought.

406
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:32,917
Critique me however you want.

407
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:34,627
But if you're such an expert,

408
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:38,005
why don't you get up on stage
instead of running your mouth?

409
00:37:42,885 --> 00:37:45,137
Was that you playing just now?

410
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:48,432
That's amazing.

411
00:37:49,141 --> 00:37:51,811
Hey, you were really good.

412
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:54,063
What school do you go to?

413
00:37:54,146 --> 00:37:55,564
Seonye? Deokmyeong?

414
00:37:57,775 --> 00:37:59,819
Hey, hold on.

415
00:37:59,902 --> 00:38:00,778
Wait a minute!

416
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:04,949
"Songmin"?

417
00:38:05,616 --> 00:38:06,951
That's not an arts high school.

418
00:38:09,829 --> 00:38:11,289
This is even more amazing.

419
00:38:12,498 --> 00:38:16,168
Hey, can I get your number?

420
00:38:16,919 --> 00:38:19,672
-You see, I play the viola--
-Leave me alone.

421
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:21,674
Hey!

422
00:39:08,512 --> 00:39:10,890
<i>By the way,</i>
<i>your cadenza sounded a bit dry.</i>

423
00:39:10,973 --> 00:39:12,016
Was that intentional?

424
00:39:21,609 --> 00:39:22,943
KANG PI-O
1ST PRIZE

425
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:26,322
{\an8}MUSICAL INSTRUMENT STREET

426
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:55,393
Hey, why aren't you playing?

427
00:39:55,476 --> 00:39:57,645
Ma'am, the thing is…

428
00:39:58,229 --> 00:40:00,606
The way you play is a bit emotionless.

429
00:40:01,941 --> 00:40:04,276
Can you put some life into it?

430
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:07,780
The notes sound flat and lifeless to me.

431
00:40:07,863 --> 00:40:08,906
What are you saying?

432
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:10,741
Focus on your own playing.

433
00:40:10,825 --> 00:40:13,661
I know I'm not good.

434
00:40:14,537 --> 00:40:16,622
That's why if you don't play well,

435
00:40:17,873 --> 00:40:19,250
we're both doomed.

436
00:40:21,502 --> 00:40:24,004
If you're so dissatisfied,
find another accompanist.

437
00:40:26,382 --> 00:40:28,634
Wait, ma'am. That's not what I meant.

438
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,094
Ma'am?

439
00:40:31,512 --> 00:40:32,388
Ma'am!

440
00:40:47,319 --> 00:40:50,156
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

441
00:40:54,076 --> 00:40:54,994
She's pretty.

442
00:41:01,459 --> 00:41:02,293
Jeez!

443
00:41:03,043 --> 00:41:04,545
-Lucky you, man.
-Leave.

444
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:05,838
Who are you?

445
00:41:05,921 --> 00:41:06,797
Oh my.

446
00:41:07,631 --> 00:41:09,258
You don't remember me?

447
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:11,677
We met at the music hall.

448
00:41:13,345 --> 00:41:14,805
What is she talking about?

449
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:17,975
I was totally blown away
when I heard you play.

450
00:41:18,058 --> 00:41:20,436
And I'm looking for an accompanist.

451
00:41:20,936 --> 00:41:22,938
So can you please do it?

452
00:41:23,022 --> 00:41:24,231
Get lost.

453
00:41:24,315 --> 00:41:26,650
Seriously? You didn't even hear the offer.

454
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:30,738
I'll pay you really well
for the accompaniment.

455
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:33,199
I said get lost.

456
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:35,117
Okay, then how about this?

457
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:39,079
My mom

458
00:41:39,705 --> 00:41:42,333
is the head of a classical music agency.

459
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:45,878
I'll talk to her and get you an audition.

460
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:47,838
The way I see it, you're a genius.

461
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:50,257
Are you going to let your genius
go to waste like this?

462
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:53,719
Genius, my foot. Go be a genius yourself.

463
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:56,305
I don't need that nonsense.

464
00:41:59,183 --> 00:42:00,142
A million won!

465
00:42:07,942 --> 00:42:08,859
Don't tell me

466
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:11,779
you thought I'd pay you peanuts?

467
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:14,281
Of course not.

468
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:19,078
Normally, I pay 100,000 won per session.

469
00:42:19,787 --> 00:42:20,996
But since you're special,

470
00:42:21,789 --> 00:42:22,790
I'll pay you 200,000 won.

471
00:42:22,873 --> 00:42:25,292
So five sessions would earn you…

472
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:28,379
a million won.

473
00:42:29,421 --> 00:42:31,090
Sounds like a really good gig, right?

474
00:42:32,967 --> 00:42:34,593
<i>You arrogant punk!</i>

475
00:42:36,345 --> 00:42:37,179
So tell me.

476
00:42:38,514 --> 00:42:40,474
What's wrong with my teaching?

477
00:42:40,558 --> 00:42:42,017
What's the problem?

478
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:46,939
I'm running an entrance exam business
and don't care about music, is that it?

479
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:49,984
Tell me the truth. Who is it?

480
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:51,777
You want to switch to another professor,

481
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:54,488
but you feel bad leaving,
so you're trying to blame me, right?

482
00:42:55,197 --> 00:42:56,365
It's not like that, sir.

483
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:59,868
Oh, come on. "It's not like that"?

484
00:43:00,786 --> 00:43:03,247
Like hell it isn't.

485
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:08,252
I don't think it's right,

486
00:43:08,335 --> 00:43:11,672
but you keep telling me
to follow your playing technique!

487
00:43:11,755 --> 00:43:14,049
I'll just end up a carbon copy of you!

488
00:43:14,133 --> 00:43:15,134
What?

489
00:43:17,177 --> 00:43:18,554
Damn it.

490
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:20,472
Get out.

491
00:43:21,223 --> 00:43:22,558
I never want to see you again.

492
00:43:23,559 --> 00:43:25,978
I'm going to do everything in my power

493
00:43:26,061 --> 00:43:28,564
to get you blacklisted
in the music industry.

494
00:43:28,647 --> 00:43:30,065
Now get out.

495
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:30,983
Get out!

496
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:49,793
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo!

497
00:43:51,170 --> 00:43:52,046
Let's go.

498
00:44:04,808 --> 00:44:06,060
You practiced, right?

499
00:44:09,104 --> 00:44:10,689
Let's hear you play.

500
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:12,358
Pay me first.

501
00:44:13,525 --> 00:44:14,902
You're something else.

502
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:20,491
Here.

503
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:23,577
I'll give you the rest afterward.

504
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:24,745
That's okay, right?

505
00:44:29,124 --> 00:44:30,000
Go ahead then.

506
00:45:26,515 --> 00:45:28,475
-Get home safely.
-Okay.

507
00:45:29,143 --> 00:45:30,602
And give some serious thought

508
00:45:31,729 --> 00:45:36,525
to serving on the gifted school
audition panel, all right?

509
00:45:36,608 --> 00:45:37,818
I'll do that.

510
00:45:38,819 --> 00:45:40,487
I wonder who we'll get this year.

511
00:45:40,988 --> 00:45:42,906
We had many violinists last year…

512
00:45:44,324 --> 00:45:45,242
What is it?

513
00:46:20,277 --> 00:46:21,195
Who are you?

514
00:46:22,696 --> 00:46:23,864
What school do you attend?

515
00:46:24,865 --> 00:46:26,533
He's from another school.

516
00:46:26,617 --> 00:46:29,077
I just brought him as my accompanist.

517
00:46:30,287 --> 00:46:31,121
Is that so?

518
00:46:37,211 --> 00:46:38,253
Wait.

519
00:46:38,837 --> 00:46:40,005
Hey, stop right there!

520
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:43,801
Wait a minute!

521
00:46:45,928 --> 00:46:48,931
Let go of me!
I just came here for the gig!

522
00:46:51,725 --> 00:46:54,311
I want my money first. It's 100,000 won.

523
00:46:58,607 --> 00:46:59,650
Here you go.

524
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:01,860
Play the piece from earlier.

525
00:47:18,335 --> 00:47:19,628
Can you try modulating?

526
00:47:33,851 --> 00:47:35,394
Okay. Can you try a variation next?

527
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:20,355
What's your name?

528
00:48:23,108 --> 00:48:23,942
Choi Jeong-yo.

529
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:26,570
Jeong-yo.

530
00:48:27,487 --> 00:48:29,323
Where are you taking piano lessons?

531
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:31,325
-I'm not taking any.
-What?

532
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:34,286
I just play the piano at home
when I'm bored.

533
00:48:36,747 --> 00:48:37,581
Why don't you

534
00:48:38,290 --> 00:48:40,375
enroll here and get some proper training?

535
00:48:49,176 --> 00:48:50,928
So that's why you wanted to see me.

536
00:48:55,515 --> 00:48:57,809
I'm sorry, but I'm not that stupid.

537
00:48:57,893 --> 00:48:59,061
What do you mean?

538
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:01,688
You're trying to recruit students
and shake them down.

539
00:49:01,772 --> 00:49:02,856
I don't have any money.

540
00:49:04,024 --> 00:49:04,858
Goodbye.

541
00:49:06,443 --> 00:49:07,277
That's not true.

542
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:09,529
If you want,

543
00:49:09,613 --> 00:49:11,740
we can provide everything,
including a dorm room.

544
00:49:12,491 --> 00:49:14,785
Our school has a scholarship program
for gifted students.

545
00:49:15,535 --> 00:49:17,537
Forget about tuition or lesson fees.

546
00:49:17,621 --> 00:49:19,581
You'd just have to focus on
playing the piano.

547
00:49:20,165 --> 00:49:21,500
And after that?

548
00:49:22,209 --> 00:49:24,169
How would I make a living as a pianist?

549
00:49:25,420 --> 00:49:27,005
I mean, people like you

550
00:49:27,923 --> 00:49:31,385
have a lot of money,
so you can afford to be artists, but me?

551
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:33,387
Man…

552
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:36,932
I'll starve to death as a pianist.

553
00:49:38,016 --> 00:49:39,142
Have a nice day.

554
00:49:40,102 --> 00:49:41,019
Wait a minute.

555
00:49:42,479 --> 00:49:45,273
Call me if you ever change your mind.

556
00:49:51,571 --> 00:49:52,656
As far as I can tell,

557
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:55,367
you've got nothing to worry about.

558
00:49:56,952 --> 00:49:58,745
Reach out to me whenever.

559
00:49:59,454 --> 00:50:00,372
Okay?

560
00:50:00,872 --> 00:50:01,832
Sure.

561
00:50:03,375 --> 00:50:04,292
Goodbye.

562
00:50:19,558 --> 00:50:20,600
What just happened?

563
00:50:21,184 --> 00:50:24,146
Did the director
just offer you a scholarship?

564
00:50:25,772 --> 00:50:27,274
That's crazy!

565
00:50:28,233 --> 00:50:29,693
See?

566
00:50:29,776 --> 00:50:32,362
I told you that you're a genius.

567
00:50:33,113 --> 00:50:36,450
I knew it. My intuition is never wrong.

568
00:50:37,951 --> 00:50:40,328
So? You're going to transfer here, right?

569
00:50:41,204 --> 00:50:42,330
No.

570
00:50:42,414 --> 00:50:43,874
What? Are you insane?

571
00:50:45,459 --> 00:50:46,668
Trust me,

572
00:50:46,752 --> 00:50:49,087
people are desperate
to get into this school.

573
00:50:49,588 --> 00:50:52,340
Pull yourself together
and think this through.

574
00:50:52,424 --> 00:50:54,593
This is a rare opportunity.

575
00:50:55,177 --> 00:50:56,511
I don't want to.

576
00:50:56,595 --> 00:50:57,846
Seriously?

577
00:50:57,929 --> 00:50:59,765
Why not? Give me a reason.

578
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:02,017
I don't know. I just don't want to.

579
00:51:02,768 --> 00:51:04,853
Why are you making a fuss?
Are you in on this too?

580
00:51:11,860 --> 00:51:13,737
Who on earth is that kid?

581
00:51:15,405 --> 00:51:19,076
It's not refined yet,
but his raw talent is exceptional.

582
00:51:19,701 --> 00:51:22,746
I haven't heard anyone
play like that before.

583
00:51:23,955 --> 00:51:25,457
But still,

584
00:51:25,540 --> 00:51:27,751
what made you suggest
he transfer right away?

585
00:51:29,836 --> 00:51:31,338
It was about seven years ago.

586
00:51:31,421 --> 00:51:34,508
<i>I went to judge a competition,</i>
<i>and I saw this kid.</i>

587
00:51:34,591 --> 00:51:37,761
<i>For some reason,</i>
<i>I just couldn't forget his performance.</i>

588
00:51:37,844 --> 00:51:41,056
<i>I've regretted letting him go ever since.</i>

589
00:51:41,640 --> 00:51:43,809
<i>And that kid's name was</i>

590
00:51:44,518 --> 00:51:45,894
<i>Choi Jeong-yo.</i>

591
00:51:49,898 --> 00:51:51,733
Dude, help me choose between these.

592
00:51:51,817 --> 00:51:55,987
{\an8}NEED CASH FAST?

593
00:51:59,449 --> 00:52:02,410
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
DIRECTOR YOON SEON-JU

594
00:52:06,123 --> 00:52:09,793
<i>Why don't you enroll here</i>
<i>and get some proper training?</i>

595
00:52:38,280 --> 00:52:39,156
Is that you, Dad?

596
00:52:48,206 --> 00:52:49,916
Hey, search the place.

597
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:50,834
Is he here?

598
00:52:50,917 --> 00:52:52,252
No, sir.

599
00:52:52,335 --> 00:52:53,837
Damn it.

600
00:52:54,462 --> 00:52:56,715
Kid, where did your dad run off to?

601
00:52:57,340 --> 00:52:58,300
I don't know.

602
00:52:58,383 --> 00:53:00,218
"I don't know"?

603
00:53:04,431 --> 00:53:05,390
Damn it.

604
00:53:08,393 --> 00:53:09,603
Come here.

605
00:53:09,686 --> 00:53:11,521
Hold still. I'll be gentle.

606
00:53:11,605 --> 00:53:12,731
Here it is.

607
00:53:13,356 --> 00:53:14,816
Good. This should still work.

608
00:53:15,525 --> 00:53:18,486
Call your dad, kid.

609
00:53:18,570 --> 00:53:19,654
Tell him to come right now.

610
00:53:19,738 --> 00:53:20,614
Here.

611
00:53:21,198 --> 00:53:22,032
That's it.

612
00:53:23,658 --> 00:53:24,951
Jeez.

613
00:53:25,452 --> 00:53:26,620
Give me a cigarette.

614
00:53:30,874 --> 00:53:33,251
<i>Kim is on his way to get you.</i>

615
00:53:33,335 --> 00:53:34,169
<i>Run away now!</i>

616
00:53:38,423 --> 00:53:40,050
Hey, what's taking so long--

617
00:53:40,133 --> 00:53:41,718
Get him!

618
00:54:02,739 --> 00:54:04,407
-Shit.
-Stop right there!

619
00:54:22,425 --> 00:54:24,386
Damn, I'm exhausted.

620
00:54:25,220 --> 00:54:27,430
-We got you now…
-Get him.

621
00:54:28,807 --> 00:54:29,641
Don't lose him.

622
00:54:32,852 --> 00:54:34,437
-Go after him.
-You're so dead.

623
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:51,181
What are you doing here?

624
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,444
Drink this and dry off before you leave.

625
00:56:05,195 --> 00:56:06,404
You'll catch a cold.

626
00:56:07,906 --> 00:56:09,199
Please.

627
00:56:09,991 --> 00:56:13,745
Be honest with me
and tell me what my problem is.

628
00:56:15,372 --> 00:56:17,415
I'm losing my mind over this.

629
00:56:23,046 --> 00:56:24,672
Everyone just says I'm playing well.

630
00:56:26,674 --> 00:56:28,176
But I know that's not true.

631
00:56:29,594 --> 00:56:32,180
I can't tell if they're clueless
or just pretending to be.

632
00:56:33,723 --> 00:56:35,141
But you know the truth.

633
00:56:36,601 --> 00:56:37,811
Right?

634
00:56:43,775 --> 00:56:44,901
You're right.

635
00:56:46,403 --> 00:56:48,863
I think there's a problem with your music.

636
00:56:49,989 --> 00:56:51,866
Ultimately, your performance

637
00:56:52,617 --> 00:56:54,077
doesn't sound like your own.

638
00:56:54,911 --> 00:56:56,913
Right now, your superb technique

639
00:56:57,956 --> 00:57:00,208
is masking your flaws.

640
00:57:01,126 --> 00:57:03,002
But if you listen closely,

641
00:57:03,711 --> 00:57:06,005
you'll realize that your music is fake.

642
00:57:08,007 --> 00:57:10,343
I admit your technique is flawless.

643
00:57:10,427 --> 00:57:12,554
But music isn't just about technique.

644
00:57:15,515 --> 00:57:18,226
You have to own the emotions
behind that sheet music.

645
00:57:18,309 --> 00:57:20,520
Your pain, your joy, your despair.

646
00:57:21,187 --> 00:57:25,191
Unless you move the audience
with those emotions…

647
00:57:30,697 --> 00:57:32,657
you'll never be a true musician.

648
00:58:05,356 --> 00:58:06,816
Do you have a room available?

649
00:58:06,900 --> 00:58:08,818
We don't accept minors.

650
00:58:08,902 --> 00:58:10,361
Why not?

651
00:58:10,445 --> 00:58:11,905
Come on, I have money.

652
00:58:12,739 --> 00:58:13,907
Just give me a room.

653
00:58:15,825 --> 00:58:16,659
Leave.

654
00:58:32,759 --> 00:58:34,928
DIRECTOR YOON SEON-JU

655
00:58:50,568 --> 00:58:51,569
<i>Hello?</i>

656
00:58:52,195 --> 00:58:54,697
This is Choi Jeong-yo.

657
00:58:57,575 --> 00:58:59,202
Can I stay in the dorm…

658
00:59:01,037 --> 00:59:02,413
for a few days?

659
00:59:32,151 --> 00:59:36,155
Given your situation,
why don't you just transfer to our school?

660
00:59:38,283 --> 00:59:41,202
This isn't pity or charity,
so don't overthink it.

661
00:59:44,122 --> 00:59:47,917
<i>Recruiting smart and talented students</i>

662
00:59:48,001 --> 00:59:49,335
<i>is a huge achievement for me.</i>

663
00:59:50,753 --> 00:59:52,380
<i>And you're a very good candidate.</i>

664
01:00:17,155 --> 01:00:18,698
<i>The phone is turned off.</i>

665
01:00:18,781 --> 01:00:22,785
<i>You will be connected to voicemail</i>
<i>after the beep</i>…

666
01:00:22,869 --> 01:00:24,662
DAD

667
01:00:24,746 --> 01:00:26,581
11:30 P.M.

668
01:00:45,725 --> 01:00:47,185
{\an8}CHOI JEONG-YO

669
01:01:01,532 --> 01:01:02,367
Attention, everyone.

670
01:01:03,451 --> 01:01:05,203
We have a new transfer student.

671
01:01:05,912 --> 01:01:07,413
Make sure to help him out.

672
01:01:07,497 --> 01:01:08,623
Go ahead and introduce yourself.

673
01:01:16,631 --> 01:01:17,674
Hi, everyone.

674
01:01:17,757 --> 01:01:19,342
Hello.

675
01:01:26,349 --> 01:01:27,684
I see a new face.

676
01:01:28,309 --> 01:01:29,727
-He's a transfer.
-He just transferred.

677
01:01:29,811 --> 01:01:30,978
What's your name?

678
01:01:32,188 --> 01:01:34,273
It's Choi Jeong-yo.

679
01:01:35,316 --> 01:01:36,526
What do you play?

680
01:01:38,319 --> 01:01:39,153
The piano.

681
01:01:39,237 --> 01:01:41,239
Hey, just like you.

682
01:01:41,739 --> 01:01:42,782
Really?

683
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:44,867
Come to the front.

684
01:01:59,006 --> 01:01:59,841
Play something.

685
01:02:03,970 --> 01:02:06,347
What are you waiting for? Just play.

686
01:02:40,965 --> 01:02:42,091
I…

687
01:02:43,676 --> 01:02:45,094
Can I do it another time?

688
01:02:45,178 --> 01:02:46,429
-What's with him?
-How impressive.

689
01:02:47,263 --> 01:02:48,181
Jeez.

690
01:02:49,599 --> 01:02:50,433
Okay then.

691
01:02:51,309 --> 01:02:52,143
I'm sorry.

692
01:02:57,231 --> 01:02:58,900
All right then.

693
01:02:59,567 --> 01:03:02,695
Let's start at page 139 today.

694
01:03:07,533 --> 01:03:09,952
"Choi Jeong-yo."

695
01:03:11,162 --> 01:03:12,121
How much?

696
01:03:14,123 --> 01:03:15,875
How much did you donate to get in?

697
01:03:16,959 --> 01:03:17,794
Piano, right?

698
01:03:17,877 --> 01:03:20,505
How many? Two or three?

699
01:03:21,005 --> 01:03:22,423
Why won't you tell us?

700
01:03:23,216 --> 01:03:24,175
Hey.

701
01:03:25,468 --> 01:03:28,179
Keep this up, and you're dead.

702
01:03:28,262 --> 01:03:29,931
Gosh, I'm so scared.

703
01:03:32,600 --> 01:03:35,978
Man, you've got no class at all.

704
01:03:37,772 --> 01:03:39,398
It's transfers like him

705
01:03:39,482 --> 01:03:41,943
who drag our school's name
through the mud.

706
01:03:42,026 --> 01:03:45,488
This one brings zero substance

707
01:03:46,197 --> 01:03:47,782
or qualifications.

708
01:03:49,200 --> 01:03:50,076
Move.

709
01:03:52,370 --> 01:03:53,204
What?

710
01:03:53,287 --> 01:03:55,164
I need to get my book, so move.

711
01:03:56,332 --> 01:03:57,750
Make me.

712
01:03:59,293 --> 01:04:00,586
Hey, hey!

713
01:04:00,670 --> 01:04:01,754
What are you boys doing?

714
01:04:02,463 --> 01:04:03,965
You little punks.

715
01:04:04,048 --> 01:04:05,216
Get back in your seats.

716
01:04:20,606 --> 01:04:22,108
Thanks for earlier.

717
01:04:22,191 --> 01:04:23,317
For what?

718
01:04:23,401 --> 01:04:24,861
You stopped them for me.

719
01:04:26,612 --> 01:04:29,365
I didn't stop them.
I was just getting my book.

720
01:04:30,908 --> 01:04:32,994
That's where we sign up
to reserve a practice room?

721
01:04:33,911 --> 01:04:35,204
Where's the snack bar?

722
01:04:35,288 --> 01:04:36,956
You don't live in the dorms, do you?

723
01:04:37,748 --> 01:04:39,834
Why is everything so complicated here?

724
01:04:39,917 --> 01:04:42,128
There are so many classes,
and they're weird.

725
01:04:42,211 --> 01:04:43,087
That's enough.

726
01:04:46,007 --> 01:04:46,841
What is?

727
01:04:46,924 --> 01:04:49,427
I'm not into making friends.

728
01:04:50,761 --> 01:04:51,846
You're on your own.

729
01:05:12,658 --> 01:05:14,243
PRACTICE ROOM RESERVATIONS

730
01:05:50,446 --> 01:05:52,823
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

731
01:06:26,273 --> 01:06:27,566
<i>The grand prize goes to</i>

732
01:06:27,650 --> 01:06:29,652
Choi Jeong-yo!

733
01:06:31,946 --> 01:06:32,863
<i>Have you lost your mind?</i>

734
01:06:33,364 --> 01:06:35,574
How could you place second?

735
01:07:09,984 --> 01:07:12,111
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

736
01:07:12,194 --> 01:07:14,488
{\an8}You really don't remember me?

737
01:07:14,572 --> 01:07:17,450
{\an8}<i>There's something I haven't told you.</i>

738
01:07:17,533 --> 01:07:18,659
{\an8}Just go study abroad.

739
01:07:18,743 --> 01:07:20,828
{\an8}You think I'd run off
to study abroad like a coward?

740
01:07:20,911 --> 01:07:23,289
{\an8}How about playing four hands?

741
01:07:23,372 --> 01:07:24,874
{\an8}<i>I'm sure you know Choi Jeong-yo.</i>

742
01:07:24,957 --> 01:07:26,917
{\an8}You're using copies
because you can't afford sheet music?

743
01:07:27,001 --> 01:07:27,960
{\an8}Don't do it!

744
01:07:28,044 --> 01:07:29,545
{\an8}<i>Why him, of all people?</i>

745
01:07:29,628 --> 01:07:31,172
{\an8}<i>Have you listened to him play?</i>

746
01:07:31,255 --> 01:07:34,050
{\an8}I hate bastards like you
who play music with that attitude.

747
01:07:35,176 --> 01:07:37,970
{\an8}<i>I'm afraid</i>
<i>Choi Jeong-yo will be held accountable.</i>

748
01:07:38,054 --> 01:07:39,638
{\an8}<i>I'll have him expelled.</i>

749
01:07:40,639 --> 01:07:45,644
{\an8}Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
